      "writtenOn": "2026-07-09T16:45:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point. I agree that Skia should not interpret `hasLength()` / `getLength()` as proof that all encoded bytes have been received. That may be true for a particular caller, but it is not a general `SkStream` API guarantee.\n\nI updated the fast path to require `stream-\u003egetData()` instead of `getMemoryBase()` + `getLength()`. This restricts the optimization to streams that expose a complete `SkData` buffer, and partial/incremental streams continue through the `SkStreamAdapter` path.\n\nSo we no longer rely on Chromium-specific `IsAllDataReceived()` assumptions inside Skia, nor on `SegmentStream` length semantics.",
      "parentUuid": "8d016c8b_37c6a8e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "d4d3d48d3873bd086a207a811f221186d80e61da",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
