      "writtenOn": "2026-07-09T14:45:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: it should be safe to call `getLength` regardless of stream type, it just returns zero if unsupported.  I think we could refactor along these lines to get rid of a couple of virtual calls:\n\n```\n    if (const void* memBase \u003d stream-\u003egetMemoryBase()) {\n        const size_t length \u003d stream-\u003egetLength();\n        if (length \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 length \u003c\u003d kInMemoryReaderThreshold) {\n            ...\n        }\n    }\n```",
